  "disposition": "invalid-or-unproven-treatment-installation",
  "root_causes": [
    "TokenJuice source metadata named the wrong upstream owner, the actual launcher/generated plugin runtime identity was not fully frozen, and realized compaction was not retained.",
    "Snip plugin source was pinned and its command corruption is a valid product degradation, but the actual Snip CLI bytes used historically were not frozen, so the generation is deleted for exact-identity repair rather than outcome selection.",
    "Cartog declared a warm structural index but the runner only dispatched the literal warm-index state; product-authored AGENTS routing guidance was also absent.",
    "Headroom omitted Serena, did not retain a successful Headroom MCP handshake, disabled its optional native plugin, overwrote evaluator config precedence, and retained no request-correlated proxy/compression receipt."
  ],
  "operational_evidence_boundary": "Provider execution and token accounting completed, but product-effect eligibility failed installation identity, setup, routing, or activation requirements. Raw history remains recoverable from the remote backup ref; invalid generations are not relabelled as baselines.",
